MIA v4 public alpha

MIA is open-source software licensed under MIT. It is an early, substantially
vibe-coded project developed with generative-AI assistance under human direction
and review. It is not professionally audited or evidence-grade.

MIA can install or invoke separately maintained third-party projects. Those
projects are not part of the MIA license and retain their own licenses, terms,
security properties, and data-source rules. See THIRD_PARTY.md and the package
catalog before installing or using them.
